<section id="faq" className="scroll-mt-32">
  <h2 className="text-xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4 md:mb-6">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
  <div className="space-y-4">
    <div className="border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-4 bg-white shadow-sm">
      <h3 className="text-lg font-bold text-gray-800 mb-2">Can I use a single contract template for clients in Delhi and Gurgaon?</h3>
      <p className="text-gray-700">It is highly risky. While the commercial terms may be similar, the jurisdiction clauses, stamp duty requirements, and governing high courts differ. It is best to have localized versions or a master agreement with jurisdiction-specific annexures.</p>
    </div>
    <div className="border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-4 bg-white shadow-sm">
      <h3 className="text-lg font-bold text-gray-800 mb-2">Is a digital signature valid on commercial contracts in India?</h3>
      <p className="text-gray-700">Yes, under the Information Technology Act, 2000, electronic signatures and Aadhaar-based e-signatures are legally valid and enforceable for most commercial contracts, excepting a few documents like wills and negotiable instruments.</p>
    </div>
    <div className="border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-4 bg-white shadow-sm">
      <h3 className="text-lg font-bold text-gray-800 mb-2">Are non-compete clauses valid if my employee resigns?</h3>
      <p className="text-gray-700">Under Section 27 of the Indian Contract Act, post-employment non-compete clauses are generally void. However, confidentiality agreements and non-solicitation clauses (preventing them from poaching clients) are strictly enforceable.</p>
    </div>
    <div className="border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-4 bg-white shadow-sm">
      <h3 className="text-lg font-bold text-gray-800 mb-2">What happens if a contract is not stamped properly?</h3>
      <p className="text-gray-700">An inadequately stamped contract cannot be admitted as evidence in an Indian court. To enforce it, you will have to pay the deficit stamp duty along with a penalty that can be up to ten times the deficit amount.</p>
    </div>
    <div className="border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-4 bg-white shadow-sm">
      <h3 className="text-lg font-bold text-gray-800 mb-2">How do we decide the Seat of Arbitration?</h3>
      <p className="text-gray-700">The Seat should be chosen based on convenience and the preferred supervisory High Court. Designating New Delhi as the Seat brings the arbitration under the supervisory jurisdiction of the Delhi High Court.</p>
    </div>
    <div className="border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-4 bg-white shadow-sm">
      <h3 className="text-lg font-bold text-gray-800 mb-2">Can an email exchange be considered a legally binding contract?</h3>
      <p className="text-gray-700">Yes, if an email exchange clearly demonstrates an offer, acceptance, and consideration, it can constitute a binding contract under Indian law, provided it does not involve matters requiring compulsory registration.</p>
    </div>
    <div className="border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-4 bg-white shadow-sm">
      <h3 className="text-lg font-bold text-gray-800 mb-2">Why do I need a severability clause?</h3>
      <p className="text-gray-700">A severability clause ensures that if a judge strikes down one specific clause as illegal or unenforceable, the rest of the contract remains valid and binding on both parties.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

